        rect (2.39599999,2.0) [395.20799999 x 1168.84] rgba=00000000
         rect (0.0,0.0) [395.20799999 x 107.0] rgba=00000000
          rect (0.0,0.0) [395.20799999 x 65.0] rgba=FF656701
           text (10.0,4.0) [143.0 x 19.0] rgba=FFFFFFFF f=17/700 "Rust's 'Vision Doc' Makes "
           text (10.0,23.0) [215.0 x 19.0] rgba=FFFFFFFF f=17/700 "Recommendations to Help Keep Rust "
           text (10.0,42.0) [48.0 x 19.0] rgba=FFFFFFFF f=17/700 "Growing"
           rect (58.0,47.0) [14.0 x 14.0] rgba=00000000
            text (0.0,0.0) [15.0 x 14.0] rgba=FFCCCC93 f=12/400 "(rus"
            text (0.0,14.0) [7.0 x 14.0] rgba=FFCCCC93 f=12/400 "t-"
            text (0.0,28.0) [18.0 x 14.0] rgba=FFCCCC93 f=12/400 "lang"
            text (0.0,42.0) [15.0 x 14.0] rgba=FFCCCC93 f=12/400 ".org"
            text (0.0,56.0) [5.0 x 14.0] rgba=FFCCCC93 f=12/400 ") "
           text (77.0,42.0) [6.0 x 19.0] rgba=FFFFFFFF f=17/700 "2"
          rect (0.0,65.0) [395.20799999 x 42.0] rgba=FFF2F2F2
           text (43.0,5.0) [109.0 x 16.0] rgba=FF4D4D4D f=14/400 "Posted by EditorDavid "
           text (152.0,5.0) [196.0 x 16.0] rgba=FF4D4D4D f=14/400 "on Sunday December 21, 2025 @12:34AM"
           text (348.0,5.0) [26.0 x 16.0] rgba=FF4D4D4D f=14/400 " from "
           text (20.0,21.0) [19.0 x 16.0] rgba=FF4D4D4D f=14/400 "the "
           text (39.0,21.0) [88.0 x 16.0] rgba=FF4D4D4D f=14/400 "Rust-never-sleeps"
           text (127.0,21.0) [31.0 x 16.0] rgba=FF4D4D4D f=14/400 " dept. "
         rect (2.0,109.0) [391.20799999 x 1014.0] rgba=00000000
          rect (22.0,22.0) [347.20799999 x 970.0] rgba=00000000
           text (2.0,2.0) [137.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "The team authoring the "
           text (139.0,2.0) [116.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "Rust 2025 Vision Doc"
           text (255.0,2.0) [72.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 " interviewed "
           text (2.0,21.0) [306.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "Rust developers to find out what they liked about the "
           text (2.0,40.0) [56.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "language "
           text (58.0,40.0) [94.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "— and have now "
           text (152.0,40.0) [180.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF666600 f=17/400 "issued three recommendations "
           text (2.0,59.0) [175.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF666600 f=17/400 ""to help Rust continue to scale"
           text (177.0,59.0) [155.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 " across domains and usage "
           text (2.0,78.0) [42.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "levels.""
           text (2.0,97.0) [3.0 x 19.0] rgba=00000000 f=17/400 " "
           text (2.0,116.0) [293.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "— Enumerate and describe Rust's design goals and "
           text (2.0,135.0) [329.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "integrate them into our processes, helping to ensure they "
           text (2.0,154.0) [341.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "are observed by future language designers and the broader "
           text (2.0,173.0) [64.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "ecosystem."
           text (2.0,192.0) [3.0 x 19.0] rgba=00000000 f=17/400 " "
           text (2.0,211.0) [333.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "— Double down on extensibility, introducing the ability for "
           text (2.0,230.0) [291.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "crates to influence the develop experience and the "
           text (2.0,249.0) [122.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "compilation pipeline."
           text (2.0,268.0) [3.0 x 19.0] rgba=00000000 f=17/400 " "
           text (2.0,287.0) [305.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "— Help users to navigate the crates.io ecosystem and "
           text (2.0,306.0) [142.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "enable smoother interop"
           text (2.0,325.0) [3.0 x 19.0] rgba=00000000 f=17/400 " "
           rect (10.0,352.0) [327.20799999 x 589.0] rgba=00000000
            text (16.0,0.0) [279.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "The real "empowering magic" of Rust arises from "
            text (16.0,19.0) [307.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "achieving a number of different attributes all at once "
            text (323.0,19.0) [10.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "—"
            text (16.0,38.0) [224.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "reliability, efficiency, low-level control, "
            text (16.0,57.0) [299.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "supportiveness, and so forth. It would be valuable to "
            text (16.0,76.0) [287.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "have a canonical list of those values that we could "
            text (16.0,95.0) [311.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "collectively refer to as a community and that we could "
            text (16.0,114.0) [310.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "use when evaluating RFCs or other proposed designs... "
            text (16.0,133.0) [310.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "We recommend creating an RFC that defines the goals "
            text (16.0,152.0) [300.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "we are shooting for as we work on Rust... One insight "
            text (16.0,171.0) [281.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "from our research is that we don't need to define "
            text (16.0,190.0) [294.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "which values are "most important". We've seen that "
            text (16.0,209.0) [307.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "for Rust to truly work, it must achieveallthe factors at "
            text (16.0,228.0) [36.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "once..."
            text (16.0,247.0) [3.0 x 19.0] rgba=00000000 f=17/400 " "
            text (16.0,266.0) [289.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "We recommenddoubling down on extensibilityas a "
            text (16.0,285.0) [195.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "core strategy. Rust's extensibility "
            text (211.0,285.0) [96.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "— traits, macros, "
            text (16.0,304.0) [125.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "operator overloading "
            text (141.0,304.0) [185.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "— has been key to its versatility. "
            text (16.0,323.0) [284.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "But that extensibility is currently concentrated in "
            text (16.0,342.0) [295.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "certain areas: the type system and early-stage proc "
            text (16.0,361.0) [274.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "macros. We should expand it to coversupportive "
            text (16.0,380.0) [279.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "interfaces(better diagnostics and guidance from "
            text (16.0,399.0) [271.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "crates) andcompilation workflow(letting crates "
            text (16.0,418.0) [272.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "integrate at more stages of the build process)... "
            text (16.0,437.0) [285.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "Doubling down on extensibility will not only make "
            text (16.0,456.0) [301.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "current Rust easier to use, it will enable and support "
            text (16.0,475.0) [238.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "Rust's use in new domains. Safety Critical "
            text (16.0,494.0) [288.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "applications in particular require a host of custom "
            text (16.0,513.0) [310.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "lints and tooling to support the associated standards. "
            text (16.0,532.0) [293.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "Compiler extensibility allows Rust to support those "
            text (16.0,551.0) [201.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "niche needs in a more general way."
            text (16.0,570.0) [3.0 x 19.0] rgba=00000000 f=17/400 " "
           text (2.0,941.0) [3.0 x 19.0] rgba=00000000 f=17/400 " "
         rect (0.0,1125.0) [395.20799999 x 25.92] rgba=00000000
          rect (2.0,0.0) [4.0 x 4.0] rgba=00000000
          rect (40.0,21.92) [355.20799999 x 4.0] rgba=00000000
        rect (2.39599999,1170.84) [395.20799999 x 808.84] rgba=00000000
         rect (0.0,0.0) [395.20799999 x 89.0] rgba=00000000
          rect (0.0,0.0) [395.20799999 x 46.0] rgba=FF656701
           text (10.0,4.0) [230.0 x 19.0] rgba=FFFFFFFF f=17/700 "Google Sues SerpApi Over Scraping and "
           text (10.0,23.0) [126.0 x 19.0] rgba=FFFFFFFF f=17/700 "Reselling Search Data"
           rect (136.0,28.0) [14.0 x 14.0] rgba=00000000
            text (0.0,0.0) [17.0 x 14.0] rgba=FFCCCC93 f=12/400 "(sea"
            text (0.0,14.0) [17.0 x 14.0] rgba=FFCCCC93 f=12/400 "rche"
            text (0.0,28.0) [18.0 x 14.0] rgba=FFCCCC93 f=12/400 "ngin"
            text (0.0,42.0) [18.0 x 14.0] rgba=FFCCCC93 f=12/400 "elan"
            text (0.0,56.0) [16.0 x 14.0] rgba=FFCCCC93 f=12/400 "d.co"
            text (0.0,70.0) [13.0 x 14.0] rgba=FFCCCC93 f=12/400 "m) "
           text (155.0,23.0) [14.0 x 19.0] rgba=FFFFFFFF f=17/700 "35"
          rect (0.0,46.0) [395.20799999 x 43.0] rgba=FFF2F2F2
           text (43.0,6.0) [50.0 x 16.0] rgba=FF4D4D4D f=14/400 "Posted by "
           text (93.0,5.0) [39.0 x 17.0] rgba=FF333333 f=14/700 "BeauHD"
           text (132.0,6.0) [192.0 x 16.0] rgba=FF4D4D4D f=14/400 "on Friday December 19, 2025 @10:30PM"
           text (324.0,6.0) [48.0 x 16.0] rgba=FF4D4D4D f=14/400 " from the "
           text (372.0,6.0) [5.0 x 16.0] rgba=FF4D4D4D f=14/400 "s"
           text (20.0,22.0) [73.0 x 16.0] rgba=FF4D4D4D f=14/400 "erping-up-data"
           text (93.0,22.0) [31.0 x 16.0] rgba=FF4D4D4D f=14/400 " dept. "
         rect (2.0,91.0) [391.20799999 x 672.0] rgba=00000000
          rect (22.0,22.0) [347.20799999 x 628.0] rgba=00000000
           text (2.0,2.0) [330.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "An anonymous reader quotes a report from Search Engine "
           text (2.0,21.0) [34.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "Land: "
           rect (10.0,48.0) [327.20799999 x 551.0] rgba=00000000
            text (16.0,0.0) [43.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "Google "
            text (59.0,0.0) [25.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF666600 f=17/400 "said"
            text (84.0,0.0) [225.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 " today that it is suing SerpApi, accusing "
            text (16.0,19.0) [90.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "the company of "
            text (106.0,19.0) [190.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF666600 f=17/400 "bypassing security protections to "
            text (16.0,38.0) [300.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF666600 f=17/400 "scrape, harvest, and resell copyrighted content from "
            text (16.0,57.0) [125.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF666600 f=17/400 "Google Search results"
            text (141.0,57.0) [168.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 ". The allegations: Google said "
            text (16.0,76.0) [50.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "SerpApi: "
            text (16.0,95.0) [3.0 x 19.0] rgba=00000000 f=17/400 " "
            text (16.0,114.0) [270.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "-Circumvented Google's security measures and "
            text (16.0,133.0) [211.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "industry-standard crawling controls."
            text (16.0,152.0) [279.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "-Ignored website directives that specify whether "
            text (16.0,171.0) [143.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "content can be accessed."
            text (16.0,190.0) [304.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "-Used cloaking, rotating bot identities, and large bot "
            text (16.0,209.0) [207.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "networks to scrape content at scale."
            text (16.0,228.0) [257.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "-Took licensed content from Search features, "
            text (16.0,247.0) [311.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "including images and real-time data, and resold it for "
            text (16.0,266.0) [38.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "profit. "
            text (16.0,285.0) [3.0 x 19.0] rgba=00000000 f=17/400 " "
            text (16.0,304.0) [308.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "What Google is saying. "Stealthy scrapers like SerpApi "
            text (16.0,323.0) [310.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "override [crawling] directives and give sites no choice "
            text (16.0,342.0) [283.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "at all," Google wrote, calling the alleged scraping "
            text (16.0,361.0) [266.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 ""brazen" and "unlawful." Google said SerpApi's "
            text (16.0,380.0) [299.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "activity "increased dramatically over the past year." "
            text (16.0,399.0) [296.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "[...] If Google wins, reliable SERP data could become "
            text (16.0,418.0) [293.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "harder to get, more expensive, or both -- especially "
            text (16.0,437.0) [300.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "for teams that rely on tools powered by services like "
            text (16.0,456.0) [234.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "SerpApi. As AI already reduces clicks and "
            text (16.0,475.0) [309.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "transparency, Google now appears intent on making it "
            text (16.0,494.0) [284.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "even harder for brands to understand how Search "
            text (16.0,513.0) [260.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "works, how they appear in results, and how to "
            text (16.0,532.0) [100.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF000000 f=17/400 "measure success."
           text (2.0,599.0) [3.0 x 19.0] rgba=00000000 f=17/400 " "
